      "text": "[i](A) 210[/i]\n\nTo find the total surface area of the right pyramid, we need to calculate the area of the base and the slant surface area of the sides of the pyramid.\n\n1. **Calculate the area of the base:**\n   The base is a square with side length 10 cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of the base} = 10 \\times 10 = 100 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the slant height of the pyramid:**\n   The peak of the pyramid is 12 cm above the center of the base, and the center of the base is 5 cm from each side (since the side length of the base is 10 cm).\n   The slant height \\( l \\) forms a right triangle with the height of the pyramid and half the side length of the base.\n   \\[\n   l = \\sqrt{12^2 + 5^2} = \\sqrt{144 + 25} = \\sqrt{169} = 13 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the slant surface area of one triangular face:**\n   Each triangular face is an isosceles triangle with a base of 10 cm and a slant height of 13 cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of one triangular face} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{slant height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 13 = 65 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n   Since there are 4 triangular faces, the total slant surface area is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total slant surface area} = 4 \\times 65 = 260 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the total surface area of the pyramid:**\n   The total surface area is the sum of the area of the base and the slant surface area.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total surface area} = 100 + 260 = 360 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\nThe total surface area of the pyramid is \\(\\boxed{360}\\) square centimeters.",
